      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="10">These also <STYLE css="font-style:italic">are</STYLE> the <gr str="7218">chief </gr>of the mighty <gr str="1368">men </gr>whom <gr str="1732">David </gr>had, who <gr str="2388">strengthened </gr>themselves with him in his <gr str="4438">kingdom</gr>, <STYLE css="font-style:italic">and</STYLE> with all <gr str="3478">Israel</gr>, to make him <gr str="4427">king</gr>, according to the <gr str="1697">word </gr>of the <gr str="3068">LORD </gr>concerning <gr str="3478">Israel</gr>. <DIV>
          <NOTE type="x-studynote">strengthened…: or, held strongly with him</NOTE>
        </DIV>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="11">And this <STYLE css="font-style:italic">is</STYLE> the <gr str="4557">number </gr>of the mighty <gr str="1368">men </gr>whom <gr str="1732">David </gr>had; <gr str="3434">Jashobeam</gr>, an <gr str="2453">Hachmonite</gr>, the <gr str="7218">chief </gr>of the <gr str="7991 7970">captains</gr>: he <gr str="5782">lifted </gr>his <gr str="2595">spear </gr>against <gr str="7969">three </gr>
